<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-VON GRUENIGEN WINS MEN'S GIANT SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-VON GRUENIGEN WINS MEN'S GIANT SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>ALTA BADIA, Italy 1996-12-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michael Von Gruenigen of Switzerland won a men's World Cup Alpine skiing giant slalom in an unofficial combined time of two minutes and 32.66 seconds.</p>
<p>Compatriot Steve Locher was second in 2:33.43 and Italy's Matteo Nana was third in 2:34.15.</p>
